    "title": "Montpelier man gets 20 years in prison in abuse case - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ben Breen ,\n9 hours ago\nMONTPELIER, Vt. ( ABC22/FOX44 ) – One man will be in prison for two decades after he pleaded guilty to abusing a child under his care.\nAccording to court records, Jeffery Coolidge, 61, of Montpelier, in 2023 became friends with members of a family who recently immigrated to the U.S. He reportedly lied that he needed to prepare for a medical exam and abused their 6-year-old son, and then did so again while babysitting him. He then reportedly posted photos of the abuse on the dark web.\nThis is not his first conviction on similar charges. In 1997, Coolidge was convicted of sexual assault and lewd and lascivious conduct with a child, as previously reported by ABC22/FOX44 .\nCoolidge will spend 20 years in prison, meaning he will be behind bars until he is 81. He is then set to be under supervised release for the rest of his life.\nThe Department of Children and Families in Vermont has information on how to report suspected child abuse on its website .\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to ABC22 & FOX44.\n5",
    "summary": "MONTPELIER, Vt. ( ABC22/FOX44 ) – One man will be in prison for two decades after he pleaded guilty to abusing a child under his care. According to court records, Jeffery Coolidge, 61, of Montpelier, in 2023 became friends with members of a family who recently immigrated to the U.S. He reportedly lied that he needed to prepare for a medical exam and abused their 6-year-old son, and then did so again while babysitting him. In 1997, Coolidge was convicted of sexual assault and lewd and lascivious conduct with a child, as previously reported by ABC22/FOX44 .",
